---
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { aiReviewEnabled } from "../lib/features";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy · Diffloupe · Private code review & Markdown diffs"
  description="Diffloupe has no trackers and is open source. Your code review, Markdown documents, and markdown diffs stay entirely on your computer."
  keywords="code review, markdown, markdown diff"
  current="privacy"
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="prose" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="h1-doc" id="privacy-title">No trackers. Your code stays on your computer.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Diffloupe is built to keep your work on your computer. Here is what that means in practice.</p>
      <section class="prose-part" aria-labelledby="privacy-app">
        <span class="icon-circle"><Icon name="laptop" /></span>
        <div>
          <h2 id="privacy-app">The app</h2>
          <p>
            {aiReviewEnabled
              ? "Diffloupe is open source, so you can read every line of what it does. It has no account and sends no usage data for manual review, and your repositories and settings stay on your computer."
              : "Diffloupe is open source, so you can read every line of what it does. It has no account and sends no usage data, and your repositories and settings stay on your computer."}
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="prose-part" aria-labelledby="privacy-code">
        <span class="icon-circle"><Icon name="padlock" /></span>
        <div>
          <h2 id="privacy-code">Your code</h2>
          <p>
            {aiReviewEnabled
              ? "Manual review never sends your code off your computer. Your repositories, settings, reports and chat history stay on your machine. Uninstall Diffloupe… in the settings menu removes the app and everything it stored on your machine."
              : "Your repositories, settings and history stay on your computer. Uninstall Diffloupe… in the settings menu removes the app and everything it stored on your machine."}
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
      {aiReviewEnabled && (
        <section class="prose-part" aria-labelledby="privacy-ai">
          <span class="icon-circle"><Icon name="sparkle" /></span>
          <div><h2 id="privacy-ai">AI review</h2><p>AI review requires sign-in and explicit consent before sending any data. When you run a review, Diffloupe copies the repository over HTTPS to the review server for two-stage analysis. The server deletes the repository, index, session state, and generated report immediately once generation completes. Generated reports and chat history persist only on your local machine.</p></div>
        </section>
      )}
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
